:: Help Company Stats [nobr] {"position":"575,4500"}
<p>The small stats panel in the middle shows how the company is doing, as bars from 0 to 100. Each stat has one job:</p>
<dl class="help-stats">
	<dt>Reputation</dt><dd>How well known and trusted the company is. Repeatable client projects pay more with it: <b>80%</b> of their reward at 0, <b>120%</b> at 100. Some new projects and clients only show up once it is high enough. A client project finished on time gives <b>+3</b>, and every day a client project is overdue costs <b>1</b>. It never drifts back on its own.</dd>
	<dt>Efficiency</dt><dd>How fast your staff turn their skills into project work: at 50 they work normally, at 0 at half speed, at 100 at one and a half times the speed. Your own Work button and the tasks of $mom.callName and $sister.name don't change with it. Efficiency moves a few points every night toward a <b>target</b> (the small line under the bar; hover it to see what the target is made of). The <a href="#" data-help="Help Company Devices">vent unit</a> sets most of it, and low Morale pulls it down. Each <b>Secretary Work</b> of $mom.callName adds +2 on top, which fades again over the next days.</dd>
	<dt>Morale</dt><dd>The climate in the office. Each employee also has a morale of her own (see <a href="#" data-help="Help Company Skills">Skills and morale</a>); this one decides how much of it they win back every night (+4 at 0, +8 at 50, +12 at 100) and how much work costs them. Below 40 it also drags Efficiency down. $sister.name's <b>Coffee Break</b> gives +2, a project finished on time +2, a late one costs 2. Every week it settles <<= setup.companyStatTuning.moraleWeeklyDrift>> points back toward 50.</dd>
</dl>
<p>Under a thin divider is your own <b>Corruption</b> bar. It rises with the dark choices you make in scenes.</p>
<p>The panel is for information only: you can't click anything in it. It updates when the dashboard refreshes.</p>
<div class="help-note">A fourth stat, <b>Suspicion</b>, joins them later in the story.</div>
